+++ b/plugin/skills/oracle-validity/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,132 @@
+---
+name: oracle-validity
+description: "Frozen bugfix acceptance, independently derived assertion drivers, executable sensitivity mutants and fail-closed completion evidence."
+type: skill
+---
+
+# Executable oracle validity
+
+GREEN only shows that one assertion stopped failing. Bind the exact ticket
+symptom, independently re-derive another oracle, test normal cases and execute
+source mutants. The deterministic runner reports observations; it does not
+certify semantic independence or human acceptance.
+
+## Ownership and freeze
+
+1. Analyzer writes a symptom ID, acceptance cases, primary driver and independent
+   derivation/driver from the ticket conditions. Do not copy the primary expected
+   constant or expectation helper into the independent driver. They may share a
+   generic transport adapter, not the expected-value calculation. Both drivers
+   must fail on the **same** symptom on the unfixed code. Record limitations.
+2. Planner proposes at least one genuine symptom reintroduction and one tempting
+   overfit as exact, single-match source replacements on the intended fixed code.
+   Normal controls must cover legitimate behavior, not a conveniently different
+   ticket symptom. The replacements may not alter frozen requirements/oracles.
+3. Implementer first commits only the acceptance/derivation/drivers/adapter on
+   the fix branch before touching production code. That RED commit becomes
+   `base_ref`; the original intake base is not moved. Finalize the plan and put
+   its byte SHA256 in `states.ANALYSIS.oracle_validity_plan_sha256` before the fix.
+   The first CARRY may finalize an unbound plan. Subsequent changes require an
+   explicit return to diagnosis, re-recorded evidence, and a fresh freeze.
+4. Evaluator executes the runner after committing the fix. Never write a PASS
+   report manually. Both original and fixed snapshots are read through Git into
+   owned temporary directories; no source checkout/reset/stash is necessary.
+
+## Plan: oracle-validity-plan.json
+
+Version 1 is a JSON object with:
+
+- `schema_version: 1`, explicit `tier` (simulation/e2e), `base_ref`: full RED commit SHA, `symptom_id`, `symptom_case`.
+- `ticket_file`: relative file in the ticket workspace; `ticket_sha256`.
+- `requirement_file`: JSON tracked in the RED commit with exactly the same
+  symptom_id/symptom_case/controls. `independent_derivation_file`: a separate,
+  nonempty derivation tracked in that commit.
+- `frozen_files`: relative subject-repo paths → SHA256. Include requirements,
+  derivation, both drivers, expectation helpers and transport adapters. Every
+  file must have identical bytes at RED and HEAD. No symlink archives are supported.
+  A subject tracking root .claude/ or logs/ is rejected before content extraction;
+  provide a committed source-only subject. Personal data is not an oracle input.
+- `oracles`: exactly two objects with distinct `id`, `role` (`primary` or
+  `independent`), `command` (argv array; no shell interpolation), `assertion_id`,
+  and `files` (distinct frozen expectation/driver sources). Identical file bytes
+  cannot establish a second oracle.
+- `controls`: 1..10 distinct legitimate case IDs, excluding symptom_case.
+- `mutants`: 2..10 objects, unique `id`, `kind` (`reintroduce_symptom` or `overfit`),
+  `patches`: 1..10 `{path,before,after}` replacements. Each before string must
+  match exactly once in HEAD. Both kinds are mandatory. Frozen files cannot be
+  replaced; traversal/absolute paths are rejected.
+- Optional `timeout_seconds`: 0.05..300 per driver, default60;
+  `max_total_seconds`: 0.1..3600 overall, default600. The snapshots are bounded
+  to512MiB archives/200000 files. These are execution caps, not quality thresholds.
+
+## Driver protocol
+
+The runner sets `ORACLE_CASE_ID`, `ORACLE_SYMPTOM_ID`, `ORACLE_SUBJECT_COMMIT` and
+executes the argv from the snapshot directory. A driver emits exactly one JSON
+object on stdout:
+
+```json
+{"schema_version":1,"symptom_id":"ledger-total","assertion_id":"conservation","case_id":"symptom","subject_commit":"<commit>","outcome":"symptom_fail"}
+```
+
+`pass` must exit0, `symptom_fail` exit1. A compilation/process/network/setup
+error must emit `error` and exit2; it is **not** a symptom RED. Wrong/missing test,
+assertion, case or commit identity, invalid JSON, signal exit, timeout, oversized
+output or source changes are ERROR. Use the commit environment only for identity
+reporting, never to decide an expected answer or whether to fail.
+
+For Go, copy `scripts/go_oracle_driver.py` into the frozen transport files. It
+selects one exact test via `go test -json -count=1`. That test emits
+`ORACLE_ASSERTION[<assertion_id>]` **only on the selected symptom assertion
+failure**. Missing tests, build errors and unrelated failing subtests are ERROR.
+The test reads the case environment to configure the same frozen conditions.
+
+An e2e driver must build/run the selected subject snapshot, enforce its exact
+symptom and own the chain/profile/cleanup. A boolean from an old live chain,
+simulation-only substitute or a declared assertion is insufficient. This runner
+does not supply a universal multi-node adapter; if one cannot be executed the
+required tier remains unevaluated and completion is blocked.
+
+## Required observations and completion
+
+Execute:
+
+```bash
+python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/oracle_gate.py" --workspace "{workspace_dir}" --repo "{repo_root}"
+```
+
+Both oracles must be RED on base/symptom and GREEN on HEAD/symptom. Both must be
+GREEN on every base/HEAD legitimate control. Both must detect symptom
+reintroduction. The independent oracle must reject the overfit, even when the
+primary accepts it. Missing evidence, unexecuted mutations or ERROR cannot PASS.
+
+The generated report pins ticket/plan, base/HEAD, frozen source, runner and raw
+stdout/stderr hashes, commands/cases, exit codes and recomputed checks. Finite
+samples do not establish universal correctness. It explicitly leaves independent
+human acceptance `not_recorded`; do not manufacture a reviewer approval.
+
+On PASS record the report byte SHA256 in
+`states.EVALUATION.oracle_validity_report_sha256`. Before bugfix completion/PR:
+
+```bash
+python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/oracle_gate.py" --workspace "{workspace_dir}" --repo "{repo_root}" --check-completion
+```
+
+This read-only command recomputes the evidence verdict and rejects changed
+HEAD/plan/ticket/oracle/raw report or uncommitted source. The Write/Edit
+completion hook also denies stale/missing/failed evidence and ticket-type bypass.
+All three bugfix verdicts must be PASS, all normal verification stages present
+and nonfailed, and required e2e chain verification PASS. The frozen RED commit
+must equal the state reproduction commit. Stage statuses remain evaluator
+claims; this oracle gate does not independently rerun every unrelated scanner.
+Direct shell/manual changes are outside that hook; the Orchestrator's CLI check
+is still mandatory. Neither check approves push/merge or skips other regressions.
+
+## Verification and limits
+
+`plugin/scripts/tests/test_oracle_gate.py` executes real Python source mutants
+and negative completion transitions. `test_go_oracle_driver.py` verifies the Go
+transport's assertion/error separation. `bench/oracle-validity/smoke.py` runs a
+real Go bug through CLI and hook, exporting a Git bundle/plan/raw report for
+replay. These are controlled executions, not a live Claude/production-chain or
+independent human benchmark.
